    {
      "name": "crt_xtoa",
      "review": {
        "ABI": {
          "caller": "Original itoa: far cdecl wordvalueBP6, near bufferBP8, radixBP10; CWD only for decimal. Outside caller pushes radix10, LEA[BP-10] near buffer, word[BP+14] value, and ADDSP,6 after return. Equality of runtimeSS/DS is a near-data compiler-model contract inference, not execution proof.",
          "public0": "__cltoasub is a shared long-value setup entry using the existing caller BP frame: CX=wordBP12 radix, AX=BP6 lowword, DX=BP8 highword, DI=BP10 near output pointer. It falls through to __cxtoa and requires the same wrapper-saved SI/DI/frame context.",
          "public12": "__cxtoa register entry: DX:AX numeric value, CX radix, DI near output offset, BL nonzero signed-conversion flag. Wrapper already pushed SI thenDI and established BP; core pushes initialDI to return it inAX, copiesDS toES, clearsDF, converts/reverses digits, popsAX/DI/SI, MOVSP,BP, POPBP, plainRETF. Not an independently callable far C function.",
          "semantics": "Integer-to-ASCII shared conversion: radix division byCX; digits above9 are offset to lowercase letters. Nonzero signed flag with radix10 and negative highword emits minus and negatesDX:BX. Near buffer interpretation usesDS; ES and DF are modified, exact valid-input/runtime ABI behavior not traced."
        },
        "archive": {
          "path": "C:\\tools\\msc-6.00\\LIB\\mlibcr.lib",
          "sha256": "03a85ba8ac1752b64c82eff829bd2de34f776630e1aa90874155b55f187d64f0",
          "size": 142539
        },
        "boundary_evidence": [
          "Complete independent medium-model xtoa.asm OMF member is230 bytes at archive84128; its entire initialized CODE SEGDEF is95 bytes, with empty DATA, no actual fixups/externals, and two preserved publics __cxtoa at12 and __cltoasub at0.",
          "All95 original resident bytes root[0x21804,0x21863) match literally and uniquely, SHA256 ce0cc5977c41eb6d3df17c85bef29b90073e2a850d5392a95f557a41cd0884e0. Both public-entry CFGs remain inside the complete segment and reach sole RETF at0x21862. Public0 is12-byte setup falling through to public12; neither is a separately trimmed contribution.",
          "Previous original routine starts0x217e6 and ends RETF0x21803. Entire member begins0x21804 with its shared BP setup reads. Unowned zero at0x21863 follows the complete member; next BP-framed entry starts0x21864. No original relocation word touches member, including straddling start.",
          "Independent original far CALL at root0x534d (image21325) encodes1fe6:16c6; exact segment-word relocation0x5350 index673. Its original itoa body saves SI/DI, establishes BP and loads conversion registers, then E9 at1fe6:16de targets1fe6:19b0, the archive __cxtoa public+12. Both conditional paths decode to this tail; no execution claim.",
          "This is the entire multi-public member, not a prefix/provider signature. Existing nofixup runtime gate supports the full public list. Review of its caller does not grant automatic symbolic ownership to the separate fixup-bearing itoa member."
        ],
